{"nodes":[{"id":"grass","name":"Floodplain grasses","latin":"Poaceae","tl":1,"xh":0.1,"wiki":"Poaceae","desc":"Grasses of the valley floor and the Lake Urema floodplain, the main food of the park's grazers.","ic":"grass","badge":"Foundation species"},{"id":"fever","name":"Fever tree","latin":"Vachellia xanthophloea","tl":1,"xh":0.3,"wiki":"Vachellia xanthophloea","desc":"A yellow-barked acacia of wet ground, recorded in the park.","ic":"aspen"},{"id":"baobab","name":"Baobab","latin":"Adansonia digitata","tl":1,"xh":0.5,"wiki":"Adansonia digitata","desc":"A huge, long-lived tree of dry savanna, recorded in the park.","ic":"aspen"},{"id":"thorn","name":"Buffalo thorn","latin":"Ziziphus mucronata","tl":1,"xh":0.7,"wiki":"Ziziphus mucronata","desc":"A thorny savanna tree whose fruit and leaves are eaten by many animals.","ic":"willow"},{"id":"palm","name":"Doum palm","latin":"Hyphaene coriacea","tl":1,"xh":0.9,"wiki":"Hyphaene","desc":"A palm of the valley floor, recorded in the park, with fruit that elephants eat.","ic":"willow"},{"id":"waterbuck","name":"Waterbuck","latin":"Kobus ellipsiprymnus","tl":2,"xh":0.05,"wiki":"Waterbuck","desc":"The most recorded large mammal near the park. Mostly grazes grass and stays close to water.","ic":"elk"},{"id":"impala","name":"Impala","latin":"Aepyceros melampus","tl":2,"xh":0.18,"wiki":"Impala","desc":"A common antelope of savanna and woodland edges, and frequent prey for lions and wild dogs.","ic":"pronghorn"},{"id":"wildebeest","name":"Blue wildebeest","latin":"Connochaetes taurinus","tl":2,"xh":0.31,"wiki":"Blue wildebeest","desc":"A short-grass grazer that needs reliable water and is major prey for lions and crocodiles.","ic":"bison"},{"id":"hippo","name":"Hippopotamus","latin":"Hippopotamus amphibius","tl":2,"xh":0.44,"wiki":"Common hippopotamus","desc":"Rests in water by day and grazes grass on land at night. Lions occasionally kill adults at Gorongosa.","ic":"bison"},{"id":"elephant","name":"African elephant","latin":"Loxodonta africana","tl":2,"xh":0.57,"wiki":"African elephant","desc":"A huge browser and grazer. Records show it eating fruit of palms and baobab.","ic":"elephant","badge":"Ecosystem engineer"},{"id":"buffalo","name":"African buffalo","latin":"Syncerus caffer","tl":2,"xh":0.7,"wiki":"African buffalo","desc":"A big grazing herd animal, taken by lions.","ic":"bison"},{"id":"kudu","name":"Greater kudu","latin":"Tragelaphus strepsiceros","tl":2,"xh":0.82,"wiki":"Greater kudu","desc":"A browsing antelope that uses termite mounds for shade, according to the park article.","ic":"elk"},{"id":"baboon","name":"Chacma baboon","latin":"Papio ursinus","tl":2,"xh":0.94,"wiki":"Chacma baboon","desc":"An omnivorous monkey that eats fruit and other foods.","ic":"quad"},{"id":"wilddog","name":"African wild dog","latin":"Lycaon pictus","tl":3,"xh":0.15,"wiki":"African wild dog","desc":"A pack hunter lost during the war and brought back to the park in 2018 and 2019.","ic":"coyote"},{"id":"vulture","name":"White-backed vulture","latin":"Gyps africanus","tl":3,"xh":0.4,"wiki":"White-backed vulture","desc":"A scavenger that feeds on the carcasses of many large mammals.","ic":"hawk"},{"id":"marabou","name":"Marabou stork","latin":"Leptoptilos crumenifer","tl":3,"xh":0.65,"wiki":"Marabou stork","desc":"A big scavenging stork recorded feeding at carcasses of large mammals.","ic":"hawk"},{"id":"lion","name":"African lion","latin":"Panthera leo","tl":4,"xh":0.3,"wiki":"Lion","desc":"The top predator, one of the few large mammals that survived the war. Hunts wildebeest, buffalo, waterbuck and more.","ic":"lion","badge":"Keystone predator"},{"id":"croc","name":"Nile crocodile","latin":"Crocodylus niloticus","tl":4,"xh":0.7,"wiki":"Nile crocodile","desc":"An ambush predator of animals drinking at the water, and a heavy scavenger of carcasses.","ic":"croc"},{"id":"sun","name":"Sunlight","latin":"","tl":0,"xh":0.1,"wiki":"Sun","desc":"Warm, bright conditions all year let grass and trees grow quickly once water arrives.","ic":"sun","cat":"abiotic"},{"id":"rain","name":"Seasonal rains","latin":"","tl":0,"xh":0.3,"wiki":"Rain","desc":"Wet-season rain feeds the floodplain and the rivers that fill Lake Urema.","ic":"rain","cat":"abiotic"},{"id":"lake","name":"Lake Urema floods","latin":"","tl":0,"xh":0.5,"wiki":"Lake Urema","desc":"Seasonal flooding spreads water over the floodplain, from about 10 km2 in dry spells to about 200 km2 in wet years.","ic":"water","cat":"abiotic"},{"id":"soil","name":"Floodplain soil","latin":"","tl":0,"xh":0.7,"wiki":"Soil","desc":"Soil that stores the nutrients plants draw on.","ic":"soil","cat":"abiotic"},{"id":"decomp","name":"Dung beetles & fungi","latin":"Decomposer community","tl":0,"xh":0.9,"wiki":"Dung beetle","desc":"Dung beetles are recorded in the park. With fungi they break down dung and carcasses and return nutrients to the soil.","ic":"decomp","cat":"decomp"}],"raw":[["sun","grass","r"],["sun","fever","r"],["sun","baobab","r"],["sun","thorn","r"],["sun","palm","r"],["rain","grass","r"],["rain","fever","r"],["rain","baobab","r"],["rain","thorn","r"],["rain","palm","r"],["lake","grass","r"],["lake","fever","r"],["lake","thorn","r"],["lake","palm","r"],["soil","grass","r"],["soil","fever","r"],["soil","baobab","r"],["soil","thorn","r"],["soil","palm","r"],["decomp","soil","r"],["grass","waterbuck"],["grass","impala"],["grass","wildebeest"],["grass","hippo"],["grass","buffalo"],["grass","elephant"],["grass","baboon"],["thorn","impala"],["thorn","kudu"],["thorn","baboon"],["fever","kudu"],["palm","elephant"],["baobab","elephant"],["thorn","waterbuck"],["waterbuck","lion"],["impala","lion"],["wildebeest","lion"],["buffalo","lion"],["kudu","lion"],["baboon","lion"],["hippo","lion"],["impala","wilddog"],["waterbuck","wilddog"],["wildebeest","wilddog"],["kudu","wilddog"],["waterbuck","croc"],["wildebeest","croc"],["hippo","croc"],["wildebeest","vulture"],["wildebeest","marabou"],["impala","vulture"],["impala","marabou"],["waterbuck"